    {"claim": "Strict liability paired with mandatory insurance and incident reporting forces discipline to the point of profit rather than the point of experimentation.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "Under strict liability, 'we could not have known' stops functioning as a cost-externalization shield.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "Claims-driven liability is blind to diffuse small-dollar harms like loan denials and biased hiring screens, where no plaintiff even perceives the algorithmic injury.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "Liability cannot deter tail harms whose damages exceed any developer's solvency, so those must be handled by safety gates and public enforcement before deployment.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""},
    {"claim": "A developer earns limited liability only by producing independently reviewable pre-deployment safety cases and red-teaming evidence, with exposure tiered to capability thresholds.", "targets": [], "relationship": ""}
