    {"assumption": "The fixed cost of preparing and submitting a safety case for independent review scales sub-linearly with firm size, so it lands disproportionately on small open-weight developers relative to incumbents.", "if_wrong": "If the review apparatus is cheap or its cost scales with firm revenue, the entrenchment concern evaporates and forensic transparency imposes no differential barrier to small-developer entry."}
