    {"claim": "Condition the liability limitation on forensic transparency: the developer who opens its pre-deployment safety case to independent review earns a fault-based standard; the developer who keeps the evidence sealed defaults into strict exposure.", "targets": ["AN-14", "AN-15"]},
    {"claim": "A no-fault pool with no disclosure precondition is the state-of-the-art defense wearing an insurance badge.", "targets": ["AN-8", "AN-10"]},
    {"claim": "The line between strategic ignorance and genuine unforeseeability is not drawable in advance by the party that controls the evidence.", "targets": ["AN-8"]},
    {"claim": "The single respondent I want is procedural — one door the victim knocks on for compensation, with recourse flowing upstream behind that door — not one substantive rule flattened across autonomous vehicles, credit scoring, and diagnostic tools.", "targets": ["AN-16"]},
    {"claim": "For the invisible band the Skeptic rightly foregrounds, deterrence cannot wait on a plaintiff who never learns they were injured; that band needs mandatory disclosure and public enforcement operating independently of any filing.", "targets": ["AN-11"]}
  ],
  "key_assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "Independent pre-deployment review of a firm's safety case can be made non-capturable enough that forfeiting the state-of-the-art defense actually attaches to firms that hid foreseeable failures.", "if_wrong": "If review bodies are captured by the firms they audit, forensic-transparency-conditioned safe harbor collapses into the compliance theater I warn against, and disclosure stops activating the liability rule."},
    {"assumption": "Public enforcement of the invisible-harm band can be funded and staffed to a detection level that makes disclosure mandates bite, independent of any plaintiff filing.", "if_wrong": "If regulator budgets and detection capacity stay chronically underfunded, the two-track structure leaves the dominant injury landscape uncovered in practice, and the Skeptic's reframe wins — disclosure on paper reaches no one."}
